---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import NeutralityStatement from '../components/NeutralityStatement.astro';
import ProofBand from '../components/ProofBand.astro';
import ProcessSteps from '../components/ProcessSteps.astro';
import CTABand from '../components/CTABand.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';

const title = 'About the Firm';
const description =
  'About Purinton Analytics, LLC: a national forensic damages and rehabilitation consulting firm founded in 2018, serving plaintiff and defense counsel.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path="/about/">
  <div class="container content-narrow">
    <Breadcrumbs
      crumbs={[
        { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
        { name: 'About', path: '/about/' },
      ]}
    />
    <h1>About Purinton Analytics</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Purinton Analytics, LLC is a national forensic damages and rehabilitation consulting
      firm. It provides coordinated vocational evaluation, life care planning, and forensic
      economic analysis for plaintiff and defense counsel in litigation across the United
      States, with every engagement built on a documented conflict check and a stated,
      checkable methodology.
    </p>

    <h2>The firm</h2>
    <p>
      The firm was founded in {SITE.founded} by Jason C. Purinton, {SITE.principalCreds}, and
      is based in Kansas City, Missouri, with by-appointment offices in St. Louis, Denver, and
      Chicago. Engagements are accepted in state and federal matters nationwide. Evaluations,
      depositions, and trial testimony are available in person and by remote appearance, so
      geography does not decide which expert a case gets.
    </p>

    <h2>Three disciplines, clearly separated roles</h2>
    <p>
      Damages cases often need more than one expert, and the experts are only useful if each
      stays inside the boundaries of their own discipline. Purinton Analytics coordinates
      three disciplines within one engagement while keeping their opinions separate.
      Vocational evaluation and life care planning are performed by the firm's principal.
      Forensic economic analyses are performed and signed by independent economist partners
      coordinated by the firm; the firm does not issue economist opinions, and the economists
      do not issue vocational or life care planning opinions. Each expert signs their own
      report, states their own methodology, and testifies to their own conclusions.
    </p>

    <h2>Objectivity as a practice standard</h2>
    <NeutralityStatement />
    <p>
      The firm accepts work from both sides of the caption as a deliberate practice standard.
      The same instruments, the same data sources, and the same reporting structure apply
      whether the retaining party is plaintiff, defense, insurer, or employer. Opinions that
      do not depend on the identity of the retaining party hold up better in deposition, at
      trial, and across the long run of a referral relationship.
    </p>

    <h2>Professional standards and quality control</h2>
    <p>
      Quality control is built into the work product rather than asserted around it. Every
      report states its methodology, identifies standardized instruments by name, cites the
      published data series behind each figure, and separates findings from assumptions so
      the analysis can be retraced step by step. Opinions are expressed to a reasonable
      degree of professional certainty and stay within the signing expert's discipline.
    </p>
    <p>
      The publication standard is simple: every report is written to be read closely by
      opposing counsel and opposing experts. The firm's principal holds credentials from
      national certifying bodies, including Certified Rehabilitation Counselor and Certified
      Life Care Planner, and is bound by their codes of ethics and standards of practice.
    </p>

    <h2>Leadership in the field</h2>
    <p>
      Jason C. Purinton serves as President of the Board of Directors of the American
      Rehabilitation Economics Association and as a Fellow and Board member of the American
      Board of Vocational Experts. He served on the Board of Directors of the International
      Association of Rehabilitation Professionals as Forensic Section Representative from
      2022 to 2024. Read the full profile at
      <a href="/experts/jason-purinton/">the expert page</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <ProofBand />

  <div class="container content-narrow">
    <ProcessSteps intro="Every engagement, on either side of the caption, follows the same sequence." />
  </div>

  <CTABand />
</BaseLayout>
